        "parms": "# ctlin and xctlin — knobs, faders and pedals\nctlin sends the value, controller number and channel of every control change, right to left. Controller 1 is the modulation wheel, 7 volume and 64 the sustain pedal. xctlin pairs controllers 0-31 with their fine partners 32-63 and sends one 14-bit value, 0-16383.\nThe first argument is the input port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. A port that cannot be opened, or no keyboard at all, leaves the object silent, and the patch still loads. On Windows a port can be open in one place at a time, so untick it under Settings › MIDI for a patch to hear it. Then come a channel, 1-16 or 0 for all, and the controller to listen to, or -1 for all: 0 is a real controller, bank select.\nMax's ctlin drops outlets when it is given arguments. Here all three stay.",
